=== meta ===
bypass: 112
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a test job that gains `allow_failure: true` can fail without failing the pipeline
origin: issue #214 G1 — GitHub's `continue-on-error: true` blocks; the GitLab spelling passed at warn.
origin2: The ruling counts it on a job whose `script:` invokes a test runner.
=== before: .gitlab-ci.yml ===
stages:
  - lint
  - test

lint:
  stage: lint
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install ruff
    - ruff check .

test:
  stage: test
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install -e .[test]
    - pytest
=== after: .gitlab-ci.yml ===
stages:
  - lint
  - test

lint:
  stage: lint
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install ruff
    - ruff check .

test:
  stage: test
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install -e .[test]
    - pytest
  allow_failure: true
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"]}]
